**ARTICLE 12: OPERATIONAL PERFORMANCE STANDARDS**

12.1 ABT shall perform its obligations under this Agreement with all due diligence and efficiency, and in accordance with Good Industry Practice. ABT shall maintain a level of service at the Licensed Area that meets or exceeds the Operational Performance Standards set out in Schedule 6, as such standards may be revised from time to time in accordance with Article 12.8.

12.2 Without limiting the generality of Article 12.1, ABT shall ensure that vessel turnaround time, berth occupancy, cargo handling rates, and truck turnaround time at the Licensed Area comply with the target levels specified in Schedule 6. For the avoidance of doubt, the Operational Performance Standards are minimum requirements and do not relieve ABT of any obligation to achieve higher levels of performance where reasonably practicable.

12.3 ABT shall maintain sufficient plant, equipment, labour, and other resources at the Licensed Area to meet the Operational Performance Standards. ABT shall keep its equipment in good working order and shall have in place a planned maintenance programme that is consistent with the manufacturer's recommendations and Good Industry Practice.

12.4 ABT shall provide to LPA, on a monthly basis, a report setting out ABT's performance against each of the Operational Performance Standards for the preceding month. Each monthly report shall be submitted in writing no later than the tenth (10th) day of the following month, in a form reasonably satisfactory to LPA, and shall include the following information in respect of each vessel call and each cargo operation at the Licensed Area during the reporting period:

(a) vessel name, IMO number, and date and time of arrival at the port limits;

(b) date and time of berthing and unberthing;

(c) cargo description and quantity loaded or discharged;

(d) cargo handling rates achieved, expressed in tonnes per hour or other appropriate unit;

(e) any delay in berthing or unberthing and the reason for such delay;

(f) any downtime of plant or equipment and the reason for such downtime; and

(g) any other information reasonably requested by LPA in connection with ABT's performance.

12.5 ABT shall also provide to LPA, on a quarterly basis, a report summarising ABT's performance against the Operational Performance Standards for the preceding quarter, together with a comparison against the corresponding quarter of the preceding year. The quarterly report shall be submitted no later than the fifteenth (15th) day of the month following the end of the relevant quarter.

12.6 LPA may, by written notice to ABT, require ABT to provide such additional information, data, or records as LPA may reasonably require to verify the accuracy of any report submitted under this Article. ABT shall provide the requested information within ten (10) Business Days of receipt of such notice, or such longer period as LPA may agree in writing.

12.7 ABT shall keep, for a period of not less than five (5) years from the date of creation, accurate and complete records in respect of its operations at the Licensed Area, including records of vessel calls, cargo handling, equipment downtime, and any other matters necessary to demonstrate compliance with the Operational Performance Standards. LPA and its authorised representatives shall have the right, upon reasonable notice and during normal business hours, to inspect and copy such records.

ARTICLE 13: TERMINATION

13.1 This Agreement shall commence on the Effective Date and, subject to the provisions of this Article 13 and Article 14 (Force Majeure), shall continue in full force and effect for an initial term of fifteen (15) years from the Commencement Date (the "Initial Term").

13.2 Upon expiry of the Initial Term, this Agreement may be renewed for further periods of five (5) years each (each a "Renewal Term") by mutual written agreement of the Parties, to be concluded no later than twelve (12) months prior to the expiry of the then-current term. Any such renewal shall be on such terms and conditions as the Parties may agree in writing, provided that LPA shall not be obliged to grant any renewal and may condition any renewal upon ABT's compliance with the Operational Performance Standards and the payment of any revised Tariff as may be determined by LPA in accordance with Article 8.

13.3 LPA may terminate this Agreement with immediate effect by written notice to ABT if:

(a) ABT commits a material breach of any of its obligations under this Agreement and, where such breach is capable of remedy, fails to remedy it within thirty (30) days of receipt of written notice from LPA specifying the breach and requiring its remedy;

(b) ABT is dissolved, liquidated, or otherwise ceases to carry on business, or a resolution is passed or an order is made for its winding-up (otherwise than for the purpose of a solvent amalgamation or reconstruction);

(c) a receiver, administrative receiver, administrator, or similar officer is appointed over all or any substantial part of ABT's assets;

(d) ABT makes any composition with its creditors or takes or suffers any similar action in consequence of debt; or

(e) ABT, or any of its directors, officers, or employees, commits any act or omission which, in the reasonable opinion of LPA, brings the name or reputation of LPA or the Port into disrepute, or which is materially prejudicial to the safe, secure, or efficient operation of the Port.

13.4 ABT may terminate this Agreement by giving LPA not less than twelve (12) months' written notice of termination, such notice not to be given earlier than the fifth (5th) anniversary of the Commencement Date, provided that ABT shall have no outstanding undisputed amounts due to LPA as at the date of such notice and as at the effective date of termination.

13.5 Upon termination or expiry of this Agreement for any reason:

(a) ABT shall cease all operations at the Licensed Area within thirty (30) days of the effective date of termination or expiry, or such longer period as LPA may agree in writing to allow for the orderly wind-down of operations;

(b) ABT shall, at its own cost, remove all its plant, equipment, and other property from the Licensed Area within ninety (90) days of the effective date of termination or expiry, and shall make good any damage to the Licensed Area caused by such removal, fair wear and tear excepted;

(c) ABT shall deliver to LPA all records, data, and documents (in whatever form) relating to its operations at the Licensed Area, including all operational data and records required to be kept under Article 12.7, and shall not retain any copies thereof except as required by law or for the purpose of defending any claim arising under or in connection with this Agreement;

(d) ABT shall promptly pay to LPA all sums due and owing to LPA as at the effective date of termination or expiry, together with any sums which would have become due had this Agreement continued to its natural expiry, to the extent such sums are required to compensate LPA for any loss or damage suffered as a result of the early termination; and
